[Host] Let's break it down.

17
00:01:58,052 --> 00:02:06,091
[Slow] 九州の北や中国地方、近畿が、梅雨に入りました。

18
00:02:06,891 --> 00:02:13,419
[Host] Northern Kyushu, the Chugoku region, and the Kansai area have entered the rainy season.

19
00:02:14,020 --> 00:02:16,060
[Vocab] 梅雨

20
00:02:16,460 --> 00:02:22,580
[Host] It means the rainy season — the long stretch of wet weather across much of Japan in early summer.

21
00:02:23,180 --> 00:02:28,723
[Slow] 梅雨は、雨がたくさん降る季節です。

22
00:02:29,524 --> 00:02:33,340
[Host] The rainy season is a time of year when a lot of rain falls.

23
00:02:33,939 --> 00:02:36,171
[Vocab] 季節

24
00:02:36,572 --> 00:02:41,972
[Host] It means season. Japan is famous for having four very distinct ones.

25
00:02:42,572 --> 00:02:48,740
[Slow] 今、日本の近くには「前線」があります。

26
00:02:49,539 --> 00:02:52,611
[Host] Right now, there is a weather front near Japan.

27
00:02:53,211 --> 00:02:55,515
[Vocab] 前線

28
00:02:55,915 --> 00:03:03,068
[Host] It names a weather front, the boundary between warm and cool air that often brings a long band of rain.

29
00:03:03,668 --> 00:03:13,123
[Slow] 前線と湿った空気のために、西日本では雨や曇りの日が続いています。

30
00:03:13,924 --> 00:03:20,475
[Host] Because of the front and the moist air, rainy and cloudy days are continuing in western Japan.

31
00:03:21,075 --> 00:03:23,331
[Vocab] 続く

32
00:03:23,731 --> 00:03:30,163
[Host] It means to continue or to last. Here the rainy, cloudy days keep going on and on.

33
00:03:30,764 --> 00:03:39,307
[Slow] 九州では、5日にかけて、天気がとても不安定になりそうです。

34
00:03:40,108 --> 00:03:45,412
[Host] In Kyushu, through the fifth, the weather looks like it will become very unstable.

35
00:03:46,012 --> 00:03:48,484
[Vocab] 不安定

36
00:03:48,883 --> 00:03:56,228
[Host] It means unstable. For weather, it describes conditions that can change fast and suddenly turn stormy.

37
00:03:56,828 --> 00:04:03,620
[Slow] 強い雨が降って、川の水が増えるかもしれません。

38
00:04:04,419 --> 00:04:08,668
[Host] Heavy rain may fall, and the water in the rivers might rise.

39
00:04:09,268 --> 00:04:11,451
[Vocab] 増える

40
00:04:11,852 --> 00:04:17,228
[Host] It means to increase or grow in number. Here it's the water in the rivers rising.

41
00:04:17,827 --> 00:04:24,307
[Slow] 山の近くでは、土砂崩れに気をつけてください。

42
00:04:25,108 --> 00:04:28,540
[Host] Near the mountains, please watch out for landslides.

43
00:04:29,139 --> 00:04:31,732
[Vocab] 土砂崩れ

44
00:04:32,132 --> 00:04:40,411
[Host] It means a landslide — when rain-soaked earth and rocks slide down a slope. A real danger near mountains in heavy rain.

45
